# 必考词 Unit26
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit26核心高频词汇

{{condemn}}{/kənˈdem/}}{v. 谴责；判刑}}{{The report condemned the use of child labor in factories.}}

{{confess}}{/kənˈfes/}}{v. 承认；坦白}}{{He confessed to the crime during the interrogation.}}

{{confine}}{/kənˈfaɪn/}}{v. 限制；禁闭}}{{The discussion was confined to the most urgent issues.}}

{{conform}}{/kənˈfɔːrm/}}{v. 遵守；符合}}{{All products must conform to national safety standards.}}

{{congregate}}{/ˈkɒŋɡrɪɡeɪt/}}{v. 聚集；集合}}{{People congregated in the town square to celebrate.}}

{{consecutive}}{/kənˈsekjətɪv/}}{adj. 连续的}}{{The team won five consecutive championships.}}

{{consent}}{/kənˈsent/}}{n./v. 同意；允许}}{{The patient gave written consent for the operation.}}

{{conserve}}{/kənˈsɜːrv/}}{v. 保存；节约}}{{We should conserve water during the drought.}}

{{consolidate}}{/kənˈsɒlɪdeɪt/}}{v. 巩固；合并}}{{The company consolidated its position in the market.}}

{{conspicuous}}{/kənˈspɪkjuəs/}}{adj. 显眼的；引人注目的}}{{The new building is conspicuous for its modern design.}}

{{constitute}}{/ˈkɒnstɪtjuːt/}}{v. 构成；组成}}{{These elements constitute the foundation of the theory.}}

{{constrain}}{/kənˈstreɪn/}}{v. 约束；限制}}{{Budget constraints limited the scope of the project.}}

{{contemplate}}{/ˈkɒntəmpleɪt/}}{v. 沉思；打算}}{{She contemplated the meaning of life during her travels.}}

{{contempt}}{/kənˈtempt/}}{n. 轻视；蔑视}}{{He was held in contempt of court for his behavior.}}

{{contradict}}{/ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkt/}}{v. 反驳；矛盾}}{{The witness's statement contradicted the evidence.}}

{{controversy}}{/ˈkɒntrəvɜːrsi/}}{n. 争论；争议}}{{The new policy sparked a great deal of controversy.}}

{{convene}}{/kənˈviːn/}}{v. 召集；集合}}{{The board of directors convened an emergency meeting.}}

{{converge}}{/kənˈvɜːrdʒ/}}{v. 汇聚；趋同}}{{The two rivers converge at the city center.}}

{{convict}}{/kənˈvɪkt/}}{v. 定罪；n. 罪犯}}{{The jury convicted the defendant of fraud.}}

{{coordinate}}{/kəʊˈɔːrdɪneɪt/}}{v. 协调；配合}}{{The team needs to coordinate their efforts to meet the deadline.}}

{{correlate}}{/ˈkɒrəleɪt/}}{v. 相关联}}{{The study correlates diet with the risk of heart disease.}}

{{correspond}}{/ˌkɒrɪˈspɒnd/}}{v. 通信；对应}}{{The data corresponds with the findings of previous studies.}}

{{counterpart}}{/ˈkaʊntərpɑːrt/}}{n. 对应的人或物}}{{The minister met with her Japanese counterpart to discuss trade.}}

{{credential}}{/krɪˈdenʃl/}}{n. 资格证书；资质}}{{The job requires strong academic credentials.}}

{{criterion}}{/kraɪˈtɪəriən/}}{n. 标准；准则（单数）}}{{The main criterion for selection is academic performance.}}

{{crush}}{/krʌʃ/}}{v. 压碎；镇压}}{{The rebellion was crushed by the government forces.}}

{{curb}}{/kɜːrb/}}{v. 控制；n. 路缘}}{{The government introduced measures to curb inflation.}}

{{decipher}}{/dɪˈsaɪfər/}}{v. 破译；辨认}}{{Researchers are trying to decipher the ancient inscription.}}

{{decree}}{/dɪˈkriː/}}{n. 法令；v. 颁布}}{{The president issued a decree banning the import of certain goods.}}

{{dedicate}}{/ˈdedɪkeɪt/}}{v. 奉献；致力于}}{{He dedicated his career to improving public education.}}

{{deem}}{/diːm/}}{v. 认为；视为}}{{The court deemed the evidence insufficient to convict.}}

{{deficiency}}{/dɪˈfɪʃnsi/}}{n. 缺乏；不足}}{{A vitamin deficiency can lead to serious health problems.}}

{{degrade}}{/dɪˈɡreɪd/}}{v. 降解；降低}}{{Pollution degrades the quality of air and water.}}

{{delegate}}{/ˈdelɪɡeɪt/}}{v. 委派；n. 代表}}{{The manager delegated the task to a team member.}}

{{demographic}}{/ˌdeməˈɡræfɪk/}}{adj. 人口统计的}}{{Demographic changes affect the labor market significantly.}}

{{denote}}{/dɪˈnəʊt/}}{v. 表示；意味着}}{{The red light denotes danger in most countries.}}

{{depict}}{/dɪˈpɪkt/}}{v. 描绘；描述}}{{The painting depicts a scene from rural life.}}

{{deplete}}{/dɪˈpliːt/}}{v. 耗尽；消耗}}{{Overfishing has depleted fish stocks in the ocean.}}

{{deploy}}{/dɪˈplɔɪ/}}{v. 部署；使用}}{{The company deployed additional resources to meet demand.}}

{{deprive}}{/dɪˈpraɪv/}}{v. 剥夺；使丧失}}{{The war deprived millions of people of their homes.}}
